/****** UP-List.mcc/UPM_List_Select ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_List_Select -- method of UP-List.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       struct UP_ListSelect {MethodID, pos, seltype, state}, the layout of MUIM_List_Select. pos: a row, UPV_List_Select_Active or UPV_List_Select_All. seltype: UPV_List_Select_Off/On/Toggle/Ask. state (may be NULL) receives the row state, for All the number of selected rows. Acts on a list with UPA_List_MultiSelect other than None only (else state 0). Redraws unless seltype is Ask.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_List_Select - method ID from <mcc/up.h>; DoMethodA(list, (Msg)&msg).
*
*   RESULT
*       0; the answer is written through the message pointers.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-List.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-List.mcc/UPM_List_NextSelected ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_List_NextSelected -- method of UP-List.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       struct UP_ListNextSelected {MethodID, pos}, the layout of MUIM_List_NextSelected. Start with *pos = UPV_List_NextSelected_Start; each call sets *pos to the next selected row, UPV_List_NextSelected_End (-1) after the last. With no row selected the first call gives the active row (-1 if none).
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_List_NextSelected - method ID from <mcc/up.h>; DoMethodA(list, (Msg)&msg).
*
*   RESULT
*       0; the answer is written through the message pointers.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-List.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-List.mcc/UPM_List_GetRow ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_List_GetRow -- method of UP-List.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       Method: read one row back for tools that drive the window from outside. The caller fills row and text capacity; the method returns TRUE when the row exists, with the cell texts joined by two spaces, the row box in window coordinates and the selected flag.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_List_GetRow - method id. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Send with DoMethod; see FUNCTION for the return value.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-List.mcc
*
******/

