/****** UP-Panel.mcc/UPA_Panel_SizeGrip ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPA_Panel_SizeGrip -- attribute of UP-Panel.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       BOOL: on the root of a borderless window: a size grip in the bottom right corner that resizes the window. The grip is a
*       triangle of dots in the muted text colour of the theme, in a 12 px square inside the window margin. Dragging it draws an
*       outline of the new window box, kept within the MUI minimum and maximum of the root object and the screen; the window takes
*       that size on the release and MUI lays it out once. Esc or the right mouse button cancels the drag.
*       Read once when the object is created
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPA_Panel_SizeGrip - access I. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Read with GetAttr/get(), set with SetAttrs/set() or in the MUI_NewObject tag list, as the access letters allow (I = initial, S = set, G = get).
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Panel.mcc, UPA_Panel_Popup
*
******/

