/****** UP-Floattext.mcc/UPA_Floattext_First ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPA_Floattext_First -- attribute of UP-Floattext.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       LONG: index of the first visible wrapped line. Clamped to the
*       scrollable range. Setting MUIA_Floattext_Text resets it to 0. The
*       paired scroller and the mouse wheel set it; it notifies on change.
*       The MUI 3.8 attributes MUIA_Floattext_Text, _Justify, _SkipChars and
*       _TabSize are accepted as well. SkipChars and TabSize apply at the
*       next Text set. MUI text escape codes are not interpreted.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPA_Floattext_First - access ISG. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Read with GetAttr/get(), set with SetAttrs/set() or in the MUI_NewObject tag list, as the access letters allow (I = initial, S = set, G = get).
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Floattext.mcc, UP-Scroller.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Floattext.mcc/UPA_Floattext_Scroller ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPA_Floattext_Scroller -- attribute of UP-Floattext.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       Object *: UP-Scroller the text view keeps in step (Visible, Entries,
*       First). UP_NewFloattext() builds the text view and this scroller in
*       one group and wires both directions.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPA_Floattext_Scroller - access I. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Read with GetAttr/get(), set with SetAttrs/set() or in the MUI_NewObject tag list, as the access letters allow (I = initial, S = set, G = get).
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Floattext.mcc, UP-Scroller.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Rectangle.mcc/UP-Rectangle.mcc ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Rectangle.mcc -- MUI class, themed spacer and separator bar
*
*   FUNCTION
*       The class has no UPA_ attributes of its own: it is used like the MUI
*       Rectangle class. With no tags it is an invisible spacer that takes
*       the free space. It accepts the MUI 3.8 attributes
*       MUIA_Rectangle_HBar and MUIA_Rectangle_VBar (a 1 pixel line in the
*       DIVIDER token colour) and MUIA_Rectangle_BarTitle (a horizontal bar
*       with the title centred in TEXT_MUTED; implies HBar), all access IG.
*       Create it with MUI_NewObject("UP-Rectangle.mcc", ...) or
*       UP_NewRectangle.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP_NewRectangle
*
******/

/****** UP-Knob.mcc/UP-Knob.mcc ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Knob.mcc -- MUI class, themed rotary knob (replaces MUIC_Knob)
*
*   FUNCTION
*       A Numeric subclass like MUIC_Knob: MUIA_Numeric_Min, MUIA_Numeric_Max, MUIA_Numeric_Value, MUIA_Numeric_Default, MUIA_Numeric_Format and the MUIM_Numeric_* methods are the stock Numeric class's, value notifications included. The class has no UPA_ attributes of its own. A drag changes the value (right or up adds; two knob widths of travel sweep the range); when the knob is the active object the cursor keys step by 1, with shift by a tenth of the range. The dial sweeps 270 degrees. Default: no frame, on the cycle chain. Create it with MUI_NewObject("UP-Knob.mcc", ...) or UP_NewKnob.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP_NewKnob, UP-Slider.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Levelmeter.mcc/UP-Levelmeter.mcc ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Levelmeter.mcc -- MUI class, themed half-dial level meter (replaces MUIC_Levelmeter)
*
*   FUNCTION
*       A Numeric subclass like MUIC_Levelmeter: the needle shows MUIA_Numeric_Value between MUIA_Numeric_Min and MUIA_Numeric_Max over 180 degrees; the MUIM_Numeric_* methods are the stock Numeric class's. MUIA_Levelmeter_Label (ISG STRPTR, must outlive the object) is drawn under the dial. Display only: it takes no input. Default: no frame. Create it with MUI_NewObject("UP-Levelmeter.mcc", ...) or UP_NewLevelmeter.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP_NewLevelmeter, UP-Knob.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Imagedisplay.mcc/MUIA_Imagedisplay_Spec ******
*
*   NAME
*       MUIA_Imagedisplay_Spec -- attribute of UP-Imagedisplay.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       char*: the image spec "<d>:<value>": 0 pattern, 1 vector image, 2 pen spec (r<8 hex>,<8 hex>,<8 hex> / pN / mN), 3 image class, 4 brush file, 5 picture file, 6 preset (MUII_ number). A value 0xFFFF or less is taken as an MUII_ number. UP-Popimage and UP-Imageadjust take it too, and notify it on a change. The preview shows the colour of a pen spec, a raised fill for a pattern or preset, and the file or class name for the rest (the image itself is not drawn).
*
*   INPUTS
*       MUIA_Imagedisplay_Spec - access ISG. Tag value from <mcc/up.h> (the MUI id; MUI 3.8's mui.h keeps the class private).
*
*   RESULT
*       Read with GetAttr/get(), set with SetAttrs/set() or in the MUI_NewObject tag list, as the access letters allow (I = initial, S = set, G = get).
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Popimage.mcc, UP-Imageadjust.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Framedisplay.mcc/MUIA_Framedisplay_Spec ******
*
*   NAME
*       MUIA_Framedisplay_Spec -- attribute of UP-Framedisplay.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       char*: the frame spec "TSLRTB", one hex digit each: frame type (0 none), state (1 recessed), inner spacing left, right, top, bottom. UP-Popframe and UP-Frameadjust take it too, and notify it on a change. The preview is a themed frame, raised or recessed, with the spacing shown as an inner accent rectangle.
*
*   INPUTS
*       MUIA_Framedisplay_Spec - access ISG. Tag value from <mcc/up.h> (the MUI id; MUI 3.8's mui.h keeps the class private).
*
*   RESULT
*       Read with GetAttr/get(), set with SetAttrs/set() or in the MUI_NewObject tag list, as the access letters allow (I = initial, S = set, G = get).
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Popframe.mcc, UP-Frameadjust.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Imageadjust.mcc/MUIA_Imageadjust_Type ******
*
*   NAME
*       MUIA_Imageadjust_Type -- attribute of UP-Imageadjust.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       ULONG: the spec kinds the kind cycle offers: MUIV_Imageadjust_Type_All (default), _Image (vector, class, brush, picture, preset), _Background (pattern, pen, picture), _Pen (pen spec only). The value after "<d>:" is edited in a UP-Field.
*
*   INPUTS
*       MUIA_Imageadjust_Type - access I. Tag value from <mcc/up.h> (the MUI id; MUI 3.8's mui.h keeps the class private).
*
*   RESULT
*       Read with GetAttr/get(), set with SetAttrs/set() or in the MUI_NewObject tag list, as the access letters allow (I = initial, S = set, G = get).
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Imagedisplay.mcc, UP-Popimage.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Scrmodelist.mcc/UPA_Scrmodelist_ModeID ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPA_Scrmodelist_ModeID -- attribute of UP-Scrmodelist.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       ULONG: the display ID of the active mode. A set picks the row of that mode (INVALID_ID or an unknown ID: no row); a get returns INVALID_ID while no row is active. UP-Scrmodelist, UP-Volumelist and UP-Dirlist also answer the MUI 3.8 ids MUIA_List_Active (ISG, notifies), MUIA_List_Entries (G), MUIA_Listview_DoubleClick (G, notifies on a double click or Return) and MUIM_List_GetEntry; an entry is a struct UP_Scrmode*, a "Name:" STRPTR or a struct FileInfoBlock*. UP-Dirlist takes the MUIA_Dirlist_* ids and MUIM_Dirlist_ReRead and reads synchronously
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPA_Scrmodelist_ModeID - access ISG. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Read with GetAttr/get(), set with SetAttrs/set() or in the MUI_NewObject tag list, as the access letters allow (I = initial, S = set, G = get).
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Scrmodelist.mcc, UP-Dirlist.mcc, UP-Volumelist.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Dirlist.mcc/--background-- ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Dirlist.mcc -- MUIC_Dirlist equivalent: the entries of one directory
*
*   FUNCTION
*       A group around a UP-List and its scroller. Takes the MUI 3.8 ids MUIA_Dirlist_AcceptPattern, Directory (ISG), DrawersOnly, FilesOnly, FilterDrawers, FilterHook (called with a struct ExAllData*), MultiSelDirs (stored only), RejectIcons, RejectPattern, SortDirs, SortHighLow, SortType (IS) and NumBytes, NumDrawers, NumFiles, Path, Status (G), and the method MUIM_Dirlist_ReRead. A set of any read-affecting id reads the directory again, synchronously: Status is Valid (or Invalid) when the set returns. Patterns filter drawers only with FilterDrawers. Answers MUIA_List_Active (ISG, notifies), MUIA_List_Entries (G), MUIA_Listview_DoubleClick (G, notifies) and MUIM_List_GetEntry; an entry is a struct FileInfoBlock*. Drawers show with a " (Drawer)" suffix in one column
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-List.mcc, UP-Volumelist.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Volumelist.mcc/--background-- ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Volumelist.mcc -- MUIC_Volumelist equivalent: the mounted volumes and assigns
*
*   FUNCTION
*       A group around a UP-List and its scroller, filled from the DOS list when created. No attributes of its own. Answers MUIA_List_Active (ISG, notifies), MUIA_List_Entries (G), MUIA_Listview_DoubleClick (G, notifies) and MUIM_List_GetEntry; an entry is a "Name:" STRPTR
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-List.mcc, UP-Dirlist.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Poppen.mcc/UPM_Poppen_Closed ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_Poppen_Closed -- method of UP-Poppen.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       The popup window of a UP-Poppen closed (its MUIA_Window_Open went FALSE, through a click, a deactivation or a dispose). Records whether the close came from losing activation, so the click that follows on the swatch does not reopen it at once. Internal, run by the popup window notify.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_Poppen_Closed - internal method. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Call with DoMethod(); returns 0.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Poppen.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Poppen.mcc/UPM_Poppen_Deactivated ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_Poppen_Deactivated -- method of UP-Poppen.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       The popup window of a UP-Poppen lost activation (the user clicked elsewhere). Marks the close as caused by deactivation and closes the popup. Internal, run by the popup window notify.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_Poppen_Deactivated - internal method. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Call with DoMethod(); returns 0.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Poppen.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Penadjust.mcc/UPM_Penadjust_Changed ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_Penadjust_Changed -- method of UP-Penadjust.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       A child gadget of a UP-Penadjust changed (an RGB slider or the kind cycle). Builds the pen spec from the children and sets MUIA_Pendisplay_Spec and the MUIA_Coloradjust_* attributes on the object, so both notify. Internal, run by the child notifies.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_Penadjust_Changed - internal method. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Call with DoMethod(); returns 0.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Penadjust.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Imageadjust.mcc/UPM_Imageadjust_Changed ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_Imageadjust_Changed -- method of UP-Imageadjust.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       The kind cycle or the value field of a UP-Imageadjust changed. Builds the image spec "<d>:<value>" from them, shows it in the preview without notifying, and sets MUIA_Imagedisplay_Spec on the object, so it notifies. Internal, run by the child notifies.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_Imageadjust_Changed - internal method. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Call with DoMethod(); returns 0.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Imageadjust.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Frameadjust.mcc/UPM_Frameadjust_Changed ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_Frameadjust_Changed -- method of UP-Frameadjust.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       The recessed checkmark or one of the type and spacing sliders of a UP-Frameadjust changed. Builds the frame spec "TSLRTB" from them, shows it in the preview without notifying, and sets MUIA_Framedisplay_Spec on the object, so it notifies. Internal, run by the child notifies.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_Frameadjust_Changed - internal method. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Call with DoMethod(); returns 0.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Frameadjust.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Popimage.mcc/UPM_Popimage_Changed ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_Popimage_Changed -- method of UP-Popimage.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       The UP-Imageadjust popup of a UP-Popimage changed its spec. Shows the spec in the display and sets MUIA_Imagedisplay_Spec on the pop, so it notifies. Does nothing while no popup exists. Internal, run by the popup notify.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_Popimage_Changed - internal method. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Call with DoMethod(); returns 0.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Popimage.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Popframe.mcc/UPM_Popframe_Changed ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_Popframe_Changed -- method of UP-Popframe.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       The UP-Frameadjust popup of a UP-Popframe changed its spec. Shows the spec in the display and sets MUIA_Framedisplay_Spec on the pop, so it notifies. Does nothing while no popup exists. Internal, run by the popup notify.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_Popframe_Changed - internal method. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Call with DoMethod(); returns 0.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Popframe.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Popscreen.mcc/UP-Popscreen ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Popscreen -- class of UP-Popscreen.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       UP-Popscreen replaces MUIC_Popscreen: a UP-Poplist (a UP-Popstring whose popup is a list) whose entries are the public screen names. The names are read under LockPubScreenList before each open, so the list follows screens that opened or closed since; at most 32 names are shown. The class has no attributes or methods of its own; use those of UP-Poplist and UP-Popstring.
*
*   INPUTS
*       Create with MUI_NewObject("UP-Popscreen.mcc", ...) or UP_NewPopscreen() from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       An object of the class, or NULL.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Popscreen.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Popimage.mcc/UP-Popimage ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Popimage -- class of UP-Popimage.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       UP-Popimage replaces MUIC_Popimage: a UP-Popstring whose string is a UP-Imagedisplay preview and whose popup is a UP-Imageadjust. MUIA_Imagedisplay_Spec (ISG, notifies) is the image spec "<d>:<value>"; a value of 0xFFFF or less is taken as an MUII_ number. The popup is built at the first open. UPM_Popimage_Changed is internal.
*
*   INPUTS
*       Create with MUI_NewObject("UP-Popimage.mcc", ...) or UP_NewPopimage() from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       An object of the class, or NULL.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Popimage.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Popframe.mcc/UP-Popframe ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Popframe -- class of UP-Popframe.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       UP-Popframe replaces MUIC_Popframe: a UP-Popstring whose string is a UP-Framedisplay preview and whose popup is a UP-Frameadjust. MUIA_Framedisplay_Spec (ISG, notifies) is the frame spec "TSLRTB". The popup is built at the first open. UPM_Popframe_Changed is internal.
*
*   INPUTS
*       Create with MUI_NewObject("UP-Popframe.mcc", ...) or UP_NewPopframe() from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       An object of the class, or NULL.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Popframe.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Frameadjust.mcc/UP-Frameadjust ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Frameadjust -- class of UP-Frameadjust.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       UP-Frameadjust replaces MUIC_Frameadjust: a UP-Framedisplay preview, a UP-Checkmark for recessed and UP-Text / UP-Slider rows for the frame type and the four inner spacings. MUIA_Framedisplay_Spec (ISG, notifies) is the frame spec "TSLRTB"; setting it updates the controls without notifying them. UPM_Frameadjust_Changed is internal.
*
*   INPUTS
*       Create with MUI_NewObject("UP-Frameadjust.mcc", ...) or UP_NewFrameadjust() from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       An object of the class, or NULL.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Frameadjust.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Menustrip.mcc/UP-Menustrip ******
*
*   NAME
*       UP-Menustrip -- class of UP-Menustrip.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       UP-Menustrip replaces MUIC_Menustrip and MUIA_Window_Menustrip: a window menu bar drawn in the UP-MCC theme. The object is invisible; put it anywhere in the window that gets the menus (MUI's Window class takes only its own Menustrip class as MUIA_Window_Menustrip). Its children are UP-Menu objects, one per menu title: pass each as MUIA_Family_Child in the creation tag list, or use MUIM_Family_AddHead, MUIM_Family_AddTail, MUIM_Family_Insert and MUIM_Family_Remove later (ids of <libraries/mui.h>; a removed menu belongs to the caller again). The strip disposes its menus. The items of a menu are its UPA_Menu_Entries array (struct UP_MenuItem: title, shortcut, Checkit, Toggle, Exclude, Disabled); to change the items of a menu, replace the menu. The right mouse button over the window opens the bar at the window's top-left inner corner; a click on a title opens that menu, a click on an item picks it. The bar closes after a pick, on a second right button press, or when another window gets active. A one-character shortcut is Amiga+key while the window is active. Every pick sets UPA_Menustrip_Trigger and UPA_Menu_Chosen of the menu, both notify. Checkmarks follow UPA_Menu_Checked of each menu. Limits: the menus are click style (no hold, drag and release); a disabled item cannot be picked and its shortcut is off, but it is not drawn grey; the bar opens with the mouse only; AddHead and Insert keep their position for up to UP_MENUSTRIP_MAXMENUS (16) menus; do not send a Family method from inside a pick notification. The strip sets WFLG_RMBTRAP on the window, so the window cannot have Intuition menus as well.
*
*   INPUTS
*       Create with MUI_NewObject("UP-Menustrip.mcc", MUIA_Family_Child, menu, ..., TAG_DONE) or UP_NewMenustrip() from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       An object of the class, or NULL.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Menustrip.mcc, UP-Menu.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Menustrip.mcc/UPA_Menustrip_Enabled ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPA_Menustrip_Enabled -- attribute of UP-Menustrip.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       BOOL: the bar opens on the right mouse button and the Amiga+key shortcuts work (MUIA_Menustrip_Enabled); default TRUE. One menu is switched with UPA_Menu_Enabled, one item with UPA_Menu_Disabled.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPA_Menustrip_Enabled - access ISG. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Read with GetAttr/get(), set with SetAttrs/set() or in the MUI_NewObject tag list, as the access letters allow (I = initial, S = set, G = get).
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Menustrip.mcc, UP-Menu.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Menustrip.mcc/UPA_Menustrip_Trigger ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPA_Menustrip_Trigger -- attribute of UP-Menustrip.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       ULONG: the last pick as (menu index << 8) | item index, both counted from 0; the menu index is the position in the bar. Notifies on every pick, from the bar or from a shortcut (MUIA_Menuitem_Trigger): use MUIM_Notify with MUIV_EveryTime, or with one value for one item.
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPA_Menustrip_Trigger - access ..G. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Read with GetAttr/get(), set with SetAttrs/set() or in the MUI_NewObject tag list, as the access letters allow (I = initial, S = set, G = get).
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Menustrip.mcc, UP-Menu.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Menustrip.mcc/UPM_Menustrip_Picked ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_Menustrip_Picked -- method of UP-Menustrip.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       a menu chose an item (menu object, item index); internal
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_Menustrip_Picked - method id. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Send with DoMethod(); the class handles it.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Menustrip.mcc, UP-Menu.mcc
*
******/

/****** UP-Menustrip.mcc/UPM_Menustrip_Check ******
*
*   NAME
*       UPM_Menustrip_Check -- method of UP-Menustrip.mcc
*
*   FUNCTION
*       the bar lost activation or a menu popup closed; internal
*
*   INPUTS
*       UPM_Menustrip_Check - method id. Tag value from <mcc/up.h>.
*
*   RESULT
*       Send with DoMethod(); the class handles it.
*
*   SEE ALSO
*       <mcc/up.h>, UP-Menustrip.mcc, UP-Menu.mcc
*
******/
